{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information for this reason includes the outcomes of each lottery and their respective probabilities of yielding a favorable (non-zero) outcome. Lottery A offers 3000 Euros with a 25% probability, so its probability of a favorable outcome is 25%. Lottery B offers 4000 Euros with a 20% probability, so its probability of a favorable outcome is 20%. The outcomes differ (3000 vs 4000 Euros), but the decision reason explicitly states that outcome differences are considered negligible. Therefore, the key comparison is the probability of winning: 25% (A) vs 20% (B). Since 25% > 20%, the reason would prefer Lottery A.",
